# Context and scope

{% callout type="info" title="About this chapter" %}
Delimit the system from its environment: who uses it, and which data does it exchange with which neighboring systems? The business context shows the content of these exchanges, the technical context the channels and protocols.
{% /callout %}

## Business context

{% figure src="../assets/context.svg" caption="Business context of FleetPilot" alt="FleetPilot in the center, connected to dispatch, drivers, the ERP system, telematics and the workshop portal." /%}

| Partner | Input | Output |
|:---|:---|:---|
| Dispatch | Orders, route planning | Route plans, live view |
| Drivers | Delivery status, photos, signatures | Route, navigation |
| ERP system | Master data, cost centers | Costs per route |
| Telematics | Positions, vehicle data | – |
| Workshop portal | Appointment confirmations | Maintenance orders |

## Technical context

| Partner | Channel | Format | Frequency |
|:---|:---|:---|:---|
| ERP system | Integration platform (Kafka) | Avro | Event-driven |
| Telematics | HTTPS webhook | JSON | Every 30 seconds per vehicle |
| Workshop portal | REST | JSON | On demand |
| Mobile app | HTTPS, WebSocket | JSON | Permanently connected |
